---
title: Customize Columns and Sorting in Lists
description: >-
  Show, hide and reorder the columns on your Projects, Clients, Companies,
  Leads, Invoices and Quotations lists, and how each list is ordered.
sidebar:
  order: 8
---
**Every main list in Taskip lets you choose which columns to see and in what order. The setup is saved in your browser, so the list opens the way you left it.** It works on **Projects**, **Clients**, **Companies**, **Leads**, **Invoices** and **Quotations**.

### **Show, Hide and Reorder Columns**

1. Click **Columns** above the list. On Invoices it is called **Fields**.
1. Tick or untick a column to show or hide it.
1. Drag the handle beside a column up or down to change its place.
1. Click **Reset** to go back to the default columns and order.

You can also drag a column header sideways, right in the table. Hold the header, move it to where you want it, and let go. A normal click on a header still sorts by that column. Dragging works with a mouse.

The main column (the name, or the invoice or quotation number) and the actions column stay in place and cannot be hidden or moved.

Your choices are saved per browser. Another browser or device starts with the defaults.

### **How Each List Is Ordered**

- **Clients, Companies and Leads** open in alphabetical order by name, A to Z. Capital letters and extra spaces are ignored, and records with no name go to the end. Click a sortable column header to order by that column instead, and click it again to reverse the order.
- **Projects** can be ordered from the **Sort** menu by name, priority, progress, timeline, status or last updated, and the order applies across all pages, not just the page you are on. See [How to Manage Project In Taskip](/project-management/how-to-manage-project-in-taskip/).

### **Reorder the Tabs in a Project**

Inside a project, drag a tab such as **Calendar** or **Backlog** to a new place in the tab row. The order applies to every project in your browser. Click **Reset tab order**, which appears after you change it, to go back to the default.
